    "chunk_id": "9744ae12-25dc-4873-995e-751a595da521",
    "technology": "arize_ai",
    "source": "official_documentation",
    "path": "arize_ai/official_documentation.txt",
    "chunk_index": 4,
    "text": "Get started with Signal\nAutomatically surface patterns and recurring issues with Signal.\nFind problematic traces\nUse queries, filters, and AI Search to surface bad experiences.\n3\nEvaluate\nCreate repeatable checks for quality. Review traces and categorize outputs with annotations. Good examples become a curated collection of test cases, while failures reveal mistakes that can be identified with evaluators: repeatable tests that score outputs against set criteria.\nCreate evaluators\nSet up automated evals so every response is scored without manual review.\nAnnotate your outputs\nAnnotate data to identify failure patterns.\nAlign evaluators\nCalibrate automated scores against human judgment.\n4\nImprove\nTest changes and measure their impact. Change the prompt, swap the model, or adjust how the app retrieves information, then run it against your test cases to verify improvement. Each run is an experiment, and Arize AX tracks every version so you can compare them and see which performs best.",
    "character_count": 994
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "be1efbc0-c3a4-4add-a342-1625f06af986",
    "technology": "arize_ai",
