    "text": "- Run Locally\n- Trace Your Application\n- Deploy\n- Packages\n- Tracing Integrations\n- Sandboxes\n- For Humans and Coding Agents\n- Security & Privacy\n- Community\nInstall Phoenix via pip or conda and have a fully functional Phoenix. For all installation and hosting options, see the install guide.\npip install arize-phoenix\nphoenix serveOr run it with no install using uvx:\nuvx arize-phoenix serveThe fastest way to send traces is to let your coding agent (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, and others) instrument your app. From your project directory, run:\nnpx @arizeai/phoenix-cli setup\n# or, with Phoenix installed: px setupSetup detects your framework and LLM provider, installs the right OpenInference instrumentation, and wires up trace export. Prefer to wire it up in code? See the tracing documentation.\nPhoenix container images are available via Docker Hub and can be deployed using Docker or Kubernetes via the Helm chart.",
