    "technology": "cross_encoder",
    "source": "github_repository",
    "path": "cross_encoder/github_repository.txt",
    "chunk_index": 6,
    "text": "train-sentence-transformersHugging Face Agent Skill viahf skills add train-sentence-transformers [--claude] [--global]and ask your agent to fine-tune a model on your data.\nThis framework allows you to fine-tune your own sentence embedding methods, so that you get task-specific sentence embeddings. You have various options to choose from in order to get perfect sentence embeddings for your specific task.\n- Embedding Models\n- Reranker Models\n- Sparse Embedding Models\nSome highlights across the different types of training are:\n- Support of various transformer networks including BERT, RoBERTa, XLM-R, DistilBERT, Electra, BART, ...\n- Multilingual and multi-task learning\n- Evaluation during training to find optimal model",
    "character_count": 724
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "41a96b03-3c31-4b0c-ad91-a2d210405779",
