    "chunk_id": "19c59589-bbba-48fb-b566-c1784eab0d01",
    "technology": "langgraph",
    "source": "api_reference",
    "path": "langgraph/api_reference.txt",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "text": "Welcome to the LangGraph package reference documentation!\nLangGraph is a framework for building resilient language agents as graphs. The langgraph package is the main entrypoint, providing everything you need to define stateful, multi-step agent workflows. The packages below form the LangGraph ecosystem:\nlanggraphThe core framework for building stateful, multi-actor applications with LLMs as graphs.\nlanggraph.prebuiltPre-built agents and tool nodes for common patterns like ReAct agents.\nlanggraph.checkpointBase interfaces and serialization for graph state checkpointing.\nlanggraph.checkpoint.postgresPostgreSQL-backed checkpoint storage for persistent graph state.\nlanggraph.store.postgresPostgreSQL-backed store implementations for long-term memory and search.\nlanggraph.checkpoint.sqliteSQLite-backed checkpoint storage for lightweight local persistence.\nlanggraph_cliCommand-line interface for managing and deploying LangGraph applications.",
    "character_count": 949
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "cb1c5365-cacc-4b48-bbde-f6a542b3546f",
    "technology": "langgraph",
    "source": "api_reference",
    "path": "langgraph/api_reference.txt",
    "chunk_index": 1,
    "text": "langgraph.checkpoint.sqliteSQLite-backed checkpoint storage for lightweight local persistence.\nlanggraph_cliCommand-line interface for managing and deploying LangGraph applications.\nlanggraph_sdkPython SDK client for interacting with deployed LangGraph APIs.\nlanggraph_supervisorBuild multi-agent systems with a supervisor agent that delegates to sub-agents.\nlanggraph_swarmBuild multi-agent systems with swarm-style agent handoff patterns.",
    "character_count": 440
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "30cb8529-9675-4032-91d6-a289af5e4e2f",
    "technology": "langgraph",
    "source": "github_repository",
    "path": "langgraph/github_repository.txt",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "text": "Trusted by companies shaping the future of agents – including Klarna, Replit, Elastic, and more – LangGraph is a low-level orchestration framework for building, managing, and deploying long-running, stateful agents.\npip install -U langgraphTip\nIf you're looking to quickly build agents, check out Deep Agents — a higher-level package built on LangGraph for agents that can plan, use subagents, and leverage file systems for complex tasks.\nFor an equivalent JS/TS library, check out LangGraph.js and the JS docs.\nLangGraph provides low-level supporting infrastructure for any long-running, stateful workflow or agent:\n- Durable execution — Build agents that persist through failures and can run for extended periods, automatically resuming from exactly where they left off.\n- Human-in-the-loop — Seamlessly incorporate human oversight by inspecting and modifying agent state at any point during execution.",
    "character_count": 904
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "44139f42-1c21-47f4-ae71-15554b78ad2b",
    "technology": "langgraph",
    "source": "github_repository",
    "path": "langgraph/github_repository.txt",
    "chunk_index": 1,
    "text": "- Human-in-the-loop — Seamlessly incorporate human oversight by inspecting and modifying agent state at any point during execution.\n- Comprehensive memory — Create truly stateful agents with both short-term working memory for ongoing reasoning and long-term persistent memory across sessions.\n- Debugging with LangSmith — Gain deep visibility into complex agent behavior with visualization tools that trace execution paths, capture state transitions, and provide detailed runtime metrics.\n- Production-ready deployment — Deploy sophisticated agent systems confidently with scalable infrastructure designed to handle the unique challenges of stateful, long-running workflows.\nTip\nFor developing, debugging, and deploying AI agents and LLM applications, see LangSmith.\nWhile LangGraph can be used standalone, it also integrates seamlessly with any LangChain product, giving developers a full suite of tools for building agents.\nTo improve your LLM application development, pair LangGraph with:",
    "character_count": 991
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "2e909c12-55cb-40db-a321-492011e122e9",
    "technology": "langgraph",
    "source": "github_repository",
    "path": "langgraph/github_repository.txt",
    "chunk_index": 2,
    "text": "To improve your LLM application development, pair LangGraph with:\n- Deep Agents – Build agents that can plan, use subagents, and leverage file systems for complex tasks.\n- LangChain – Provides integrations and composable components to streamline LLM application development.\n- LangSmith – Helpful for agent evals and observability. Debug poor-performing LLM app runs, evaluate agent trajectories, gain visibility in production, and improve performance over time.\n- LangSmith Deployment – Deploy and scale agents effortlessly with a purpose-built deployment platform for long-running, stateful workflows. Discover, reuse, configure, and share agents across teams – and iterate quickly with visual prototyping in LangSmith Studio.\n- docs.langchain.com – Comprehensive documentation, including conceptual overviews and guides\n- reference.langchain.com/python/langgraph – API reference docs for LangGraph packages\n- LangGraph Quickstart – Get started building with LangGraph",
    "character_count": 970
  },
  {
