  {
    "chunk_id": "07278768-50a3-433b-bfbc-e39058089acf",
    "technology": "llama_cpp",
    "source": "github_repository",
    "path": "llama_cpp/github_repository.txt",
    "chunk_index": 10,
    "text": "After downloading a model, use the CLI tools to run it locally - see below.\nllama.cpp requires the model to be stored in the GGUF file format. Models in other data formats can be converted to GGUF using the convert_*.py Python scripts in this repo.\nThe Hugging Face platform provides a variety of online tools for converting, quantizing and hosting models with llama.cpp:\n- Use the GGUF-my-repo space to convert to GGUF format and quantize model weights to smaller sizes\n- Use the GGUF-my-LoRA space to convert LoRA adapters to GGUF format (more info: #10123)\n- Use the GGUF-editor space to edit GGUF meta data in the browser (more info: #9268)\n- Use the Inference Endpoints to directly host llama.cppin the cloud (more info: #9669)\nTo learn more about model quantization, read this documentation\n-",
