    "chunk_id": "a668342b-e59c-43ea-acbc-8f92525282ef",
    "technology": "llama_cpp",
    "source": "official_documentation",
    "path": "llama_cpp/official_documentation.txt",
    "chunk_index": 12,
    "text": "-\nRun in conversation mode with custom chat template# use the \"chatml\" template (use -h to see the list of supported templates) llama-cli -m model.gguf -cnv --chat-template chatml # use a custom template llama-cli -m model.gguf -cnv --in-prefix 'User: ' --reverse-prompt 'User:'\n-\nConstrain the output with a custom grammarllama-cli -m model.gguf -n 256 --grammar-file grammars/json.gbnf -p 'Request: schedule a call at 8pm; Command:' # {\"appointmentTime\": \"8pm\", \"appointmentDetails\": \"schedule a a call\"} The grammars/ folder contains a handful of sample grammars. To write your own, check out the GBNF Guide. For authoring more complex JSON grammars, check out https://grammar.intrinsiclabs.ai/\nA lightweight, OpenAI API compatible, HTTP server for serving LLMs.\n-",
    "character_count": 767
