    "text": "[24/03/31] We supported ORPO. See examples for usage.\n[24/03/21] Our paper \"LlamaFactory: Unified Efficient Fine-Tuning of 100+ Language Models\" is available at arXiv!\n[24/03/20] We supported FSDP+QLoRA that fine-tunes a 70B model on 2x24GB GPUs. See examples for usage.\n[24/03/13] We supported LoRA+. See examples for usage.\n[24/03/07] We supported GaLore optimizer. See examples for usage.\n[24/03/07] We integrated vLLM for faster and concurrent inference. Try infer_backend: vllm to enjoy 270% inference speed.\n[24/02/28] We supported weight-decomposed LoRA (DoRA). Try use_dora: true to activate DoRA training.\n[24/02/15] We supported block expansion proposed by LLaMA Pro. See examples for usage.\n[24/02/05] Qwen1.5 (Qwen2 beta version) series models are supported in LLaMA-Factory. Check this blog post for details.\n[24/01/18] We supported agent tuning for most models, equipping model with tool using abilities by fine-tuning with dataset: glaive_toolcall_en.",
    "character_count": 966
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "9469fb67-cdd2-4157-85b8-1e2d2e8b2f07",
    "technology": "llama_factory",
    "source": "github_repository",
    "path": "llama_factory/github_repository.txt",
    "chunk_index": 10,
    "text": "[24/01/18] We supported agent tuning for most models, equipping model with tool using abilities by fine-tuning with dataset: glaive_toolcall_en.\n[23/12/23] We supported unsloth's implementation to boost LoRA tuning for the LLaMA, Mistral and Yi models. Try use_unsloth: true argument to activate unsloth patch. It achieves 170% speed in our benchmark, check this page for details.\n[23/12/12] We supported fine-tuning the latest MoE model Mixtral 8x7B in our framework. See hardware requirement here.\n[23/12/01] We supported downloading pre-trained models and datasets from the ModelScope Hub. See this tutorial for usage.\n[23/10/21] We supported NEFTune trick for fine-tuning. Try neftune_noise_alpha: 5 argument to activate NEFTune.\n[23/09/27] We supported shift_attn: true argument to enable shift short attention.\n[23/09/23] We integrated MMLU, C-Eval and CMMLU benchmarks in this repo. See examples for usage.",
    "character_count": 913
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "07950c18-906b-476e-9d59-99361e93c895",
    "technology": "llama_factory",
