    "chunk_id": "5346a3c1-85b5-462f-85f8-14c7318c0605",
    "technology": "nvidia_triton_inference_server",
    "source": "github_repository",
    "path": "nvidia_triton_inference_server/github_repository.txt",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "text": "Warning\nYou are currently on the main branch which tracks under-development progress\ntowards the next release. The current release is version 2.70.0\nand corresponds to the 26.06 container release on NVIDIA GPU Cloud (NGC).\nTriton Inference Server is an open source inference serving software that streamlines AI inferencing. Triton enables teams to deploy any AI model from multiple deep learning and machine learning frameworks, including TensorRT, PyTorch, ONNX, OpenVINO, Python, RAPIDS FIL, and more. Triton Inference Server supports inference across cloud, data center, edge and embedded devices on NVIDIA GPUs, x86 and ARM CPU, or AWS Inferentia. Triton Inference Server delivers optimized performance for many query types, including real time, batched, ensembles and audio/video streaming. Triton inference Server is part of NVIDIA AI Enterprise, a software platform that accelerates the data science pipeline and streamlines the development and deployment of production AI.",
    "character_count": 981
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "aac36e61-19e9-4028-8f47-fe7c4020073d",
    "technology": "nvidia_triton_inference_server",
    "source": "github_repository",
    "path": "nvidia_triton_inference_server/github_repository.txt",
    "chunk_index": 1,
    "text": "Major features include:\n- Supports multiple deep learning frameworks\n- Supports multiple machine learning frameworks\n- Concurrent model execution\n- Dynamic batching\n- Sequence batching and implicit state management for stateful models\n- Provides Backend API that allows adding custom backends and pre/post processing operations\n- Supports writing custom backends in python, a.k.a. Python-based backends.\n- Model pipelines using Ensembling or Business Logic Scripting (BLS)\n- HTTP/REST and GRPC inference protocols based on the community developed KServe protocol\n- A C API and Java API allow Triton to link directly into your application for edge and other in-process use cases\n- Metrics indicating GPU utilization, server throughput, server latency, and more\nNew to Triton Inference Server? Make use of these tutorials to begin your Triton journey!",
    "character_count": 849
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "aca6c0f8-216e-4bcf-aec0-0a3367c0347d",
