  {
    "chunk_id": "7ff63ef8-0f17-4bad-95a8-f1e81128f40a",
    "technology": "openai_gpt",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.txt",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "text": "Changelog\nJuly, 2026\nReleased GPT Transcribe for accurate file transcription and final transcripts of committed Realtime turns, along with GPT Live Transcribe for low-latency streaming transcription.\nBoth models support free-form transcription context, keyword hints, and multiple expected input languages. Compare supported outputs and workflows in the transcription guide.\nAdded hard spend limits for organizations and projects on the OpenAI API platform. Set a monthly cap that causes affected API requests to return a 429 error when tracked spend reaches the limit. Use spend alerts for notification before traffic is interrupted. Read more in the spend limits guide.\nReleased the GPT-5.6 model family, including GPT-5.6 Sol for frontier capability, GPT-5.6 Terra for a balance of intelligence and cost, and GPT-5.6 Luna for efficient, high-volume workloads. The gpt-5.6 alias routes requests to gpt-5.6-sol.",
    "character_count": 912
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "436c6e01-1224-4f57-a955-69f071fe2c5f",
    "technology": "openai_gpt",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.txt",
    "chunk_index": 1,
    "text": "GPT-5.6 adds Programmatic Tool Calling, explicit prompt caching controls, persisted reasoning, max reasoning effort, and Pro mode, and Multi-agent orchestration in beta for the Responses API. GPT-5.6 also accepts images at their original dimensions with original or auto image detail.\nReleased GPT-Realtime-2.1, an updated realtime reasoning model with improved alphanumeric recognition, silence and noise handling, and interruption behavior. Also released GPT-Realtime-2.1 mini, a faster, lower-cost distilled reasoning model for realtime voice applications.\nJune, 2026\nUpdated the chat-latest snapshot, which points to the latest Instant model currently used in ChatGPT. We recommend leveraging GPT-5.5 for production API usage, but feel free to use this model to test the latest improvements for chat use cases. The underlying model snapshot will be regularly updated. Read more here.",
    "character_count": 887
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "261fddc2-8869-4d48-96e0-b2a21777f072",
    "technology": "openai_gpt",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.txt",
    "chunk_index": 2,
    "text": "Released the Safety Usage Dashboard on the OpenAI API platform. The Safety dashboard shows blocked Responses requests based on safety_identifier values sent on requests to identify end users. Visit the Safety dashboard.\nWeb search can now return image results alongside regular text results. Use image search when your application needs current or web-grounded visuals, such as product photos, landmarks, places, events, or visual references. Read more in the web search guide.\nReleased a redesigned navigation for the OpenAI API platform, visit here.\nAdded moderation scores to the Responses API and Chat Completions API. Pass a moderation object in a generation request to receive moderation results for both the model input and generated output in the same response.\nLearn more in the Moderation guide.\nAnnounced the deprecation of reusable prompt objects, the Evals platform, and Agent Builder. See the deprecations page for shutdown timelines and migration guidance.",
    "character_count": 971
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "766601de-8194-4d1b-b21b-5d23ca3dc872",
    "technology": "openai_gpt",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.txt",
    "chunk_index": 3,
    "text": "Announced the deprecation of reusable prompt objects, the Evals platform, and Agent Builder. See the deprecations page for shutdown timelines and migration guidance.\nStarting June 2, 2026, eligible container sessions will be billed per minute with a 5-minute minimum, instead of being billed at the full 20-minute session rate. The underlying per-minute rate will remain the same.\nThis update is intended to make billing more granular for shorter sessions and will lower effective cost for customers.\nYou can find current built-in tool pricing in our API pricing docs.\nOpenAI models are now available in Amazon Bedrock through an OpenAI-compatible Responses API endpoint. Supported models and features vary by AWS Region. Learn more.\nMay, 2026\nFor organizations without ZDR enabled, prompt_cache_retention now defaults to 24h instead of in_memory, enabling extended prompt caching by default. Learn more.",
    "character_count": 904
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "712bc0f2-642f-4a27-a3df-6ce86f70eaba",
    "technology": "openai_gpt",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.txt",
    "chunk_index": 4,
    "text": "May, 2026\nFor organizations without ZDR enabled, prompt_cache_retention now defaults to 24h instead of in_memory, enabling extended prompt caching by default. Learn more.\nReleased chat-latest snapshot which points to the latest Instant model currently used in ChatGPT. We recommend leveraging GPT-5.5 for production API usage, but feel free to use this model to test the latest improvements for chat use cases. The underlying model snapshot will be regularly updated. Read more here.\nReleased workload identity federation. Trusted workloads can exchange externally issued identity tokens for short-lived OpenAI access tokens without storing long-lived API keys.\nAdded new Admin API capabilities for managing spend alerts, model allowlists, data retention settings, and hosted tool permissions, plus querying granular billing line items.",
    "character_count": 836
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "40762c7a-992e-4677-bd35-b276f8a57f78",
    "technology": "openai_gpt",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.txt",
    "chunk_index": 5,
    "text": "Added new Admin API capabilities for managing spend alerts, model allowlists, data retention settings, and hosted tool permissions, plus querying granular billing line items.\nReleased Secure MCP Tunnel for enterprise customers. Secure MCP Tunnel lets supported OpenAI products including ChatGPT web, Codex, Responses API, and AgentKit connect to private or on-prem MCP servers through a customer-hosted tunnel-client without exposing those servers to the public internet.\nYou can now manage multiple IP allowlists and apply each one at the project level or across the whole organization. To configure them, go to Settings > Security > IP allowlist.\nDeprecated DALL·E model snapshots and the Realtime API Beta.\nDALL·E model snapshots dall-e-2 and dall-e-3 were deprecated and removed from the API on May 12, 2026. We recommend using gpt-image-2, gpt-image-1, or gpt-image-1-mini instead.",
    "character_count": 886
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "fe616820-826a-49df-ac7f-3b1c3377ff39",
    "technology": "openai_gpt",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.txt",
    "chunk_index": 6,
    "text": "DALL·E model snapshots dall-e-2 and dall-e-3 were deprecated and removed from the API on May 12, 2026. We recommend using gpt-image-2, gpt-image-1, or gpt-image-1-mini instead.\nThe Realtime API Beta was deprecated and removed from the API on May 12, 2026. If you are still using the beta interface, migrate to the released Realtime API. See the migration guide and the full deprecations page.\nAdded return_token_budget for the Responses API web search tool. Use it to opt in to longer GPT-5+ reasoning web search runs for high-effort research and evaluation workloads.\nReleased GPT-Realtime-2, a new realtime voice model with configurable reasoning for speech-to-speech agents, along with GPT-Realtime-Translate for streaming speech translation and GPT-Realtime-Whisper for streaming speech-to-text.",
    "character_count": 799
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "835ea944-16d7-41a0-a02e-727247331037",
    "technology": "openai_gpt",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.txt",
    "chunk_index": 7,
    "text": "Updated the Realtime and audio guide, added a dedicated Realtime translation guide, refreshed Realtime transcription for streaming transcripts, and moved realtime prompting guidance into Using realtime models.\nReleased the OpenAI Developers plugin for Codex. This helps you build AI applications and agents in Codex with OpenAI Platform access and OpenAI API setup guidance.\nThe updated Agents SDK is now available in TypeScript, with support for sandbox agents and an open-source harness built in. Learn more here.\nReleased chat-latest snapshot which points to the latest Instant model currently used in ChatGPT. We recommend leveraging GPT-5.5 for production API usage, but feel free to use this model to test our latest improvements for chat use cases. The underlying model snapshot will be regularly updated. Read more here.\nAdmin APIs are now supported in the OpenAI SDKs for Node, Python, Go, Ruby, and Java. See the Admin APIs guide for setup instructions and examples.\nApril, 2026",
    "character_count": 988
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "58a96a03-4596-4f10-87fb-9bcb1c843dc9",
    "technology": "openai_gpt",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.txt",
    "chunk_index": 8,
    "text": "Admin APIs are now supported in the OpenAI SDKs for Node, Python, Go, Ruby, and Java. See the Admin APIs guide for setup instructions and examples.\nApril, 2026\nReleased GPT-5.5, a new frontier model for complex professional work, to the Chat Completions and Responses API, and released GPT-5.5 Pro for Responses API requests for tougher problems that benefit from more compute.\nGPT-5.5 supports a 1M token context window, image input, structured outputs, function calling, prompt caching, Batch, tool search, built-in computer use, hosted shell, apply patch, Skills, MCP, and web search. Key updates include:\n- Reasoning effort now defaults to medium.\n- When image_detailis unset or set toauto, the model now uses original behavior.\n- Caching for GPT-5.5 only works with extended prompt caching. In-memory prompt caching is not supported. Learn more here.",
    "character_count": 855
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "2b9fefd9-0d62-4907-930f-b21e9b3f3a4a",
    "technology": "openai_gpt",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.txt",
    "chunk_index": 9,
    "text": "- Caching for GPT-5.5 only works with extended prompt caching. In-memory prompt caching is not supported. Learn more here.\nReleased GPT Image 2, a state-of-the-art image generation model for image generation and editing. GPT Image 2 supports flexible image sizes, high-fidelity image inputs, token-based image pricing, and Batch API support with a 50% discount.\nUpdated the Agents SDK with new capabilities, including:\n- running agents in controlled sandboxes;\n- inspecting and customizing the open-source harness; and\n- controlling when memories are created and where they're stored.\nMarch, 2026\nReleased GPT-5.4 mini and GPT-5.4 nano to the Chat Completions and Responses API. GPT-5.4 mini brings GPT-5.4-class capabilities to a faster, more efficient model for high-volume workloads, while GPT-5.4 nano is optimized for simple high-volume tasks where speed and cost matter most.",
    "character_count": 881
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "70de7cf0-c553-4689-97ed-41d32edfa0be",
    "technology": "openai_gpt",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.txt",
    "chunk_index": 10,
    "text": "GPT-5.4 mini supports tool search, built-in computer use, and compaction. GPT-5.4 nano supports compaction, but does not support tool search or computer use.\nUpdated the gpt-5.3-chat-latest slug to point to the latest model currently used in ChatGPT.\nUpdated our image encoder to fix a small bug with input_image inputs in GPT-5.4. Some image understanding use cases may now see improved quality. No action is required.\nExpanded the Sora API with reusable character references, longer generations up to 20 seconds, 1080p output for sora-2-pro, video extensions, and Batch API support for POST /v1/videos. 1080p generations on sora-2-pro are billed at $0.70 per second. Learn more here.\nAdded POST /v1/videos/edits for editing existing videos. This will replace POST /v1/videos/{video_id}/remix, which will be deprecated in 6 months. Learn more here.",
    "character_count": 849
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "f7b588da-1c0e-48bd-baec-ab7cf07279a6",
    "technology": "openai_gpt",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.txt",
    "chunk_index": 11,
    "text": "Added POST /v1/videos/edits for editing existing videos. This will replace POST /v1/videos/{video_id}/remix, which will be deprecated in 6 months. Learn more here.\nReleased GPT-5.4, our newest frontier model for professional work, to the Chat Completions and Responses API, and released GPT-5.4 Pro to the Responses API for tougher problems that benefit from more compute.\nAlso released:\n- Tool search in the Responses API, which lets models defer large tool surfaces until runtime to reduce token usage, preserve cache performance, and improve latency.\n- Built-in Computer use support in GPT-5.4 through the Responses API computertool for screenshot-based UI interaction.\n- A 1M token context window and native Compaction support for longer-running agent workflows.\nReleased gpt-5.3-chat-latest to the Chat Completions and Responses API. This model points to the GPT-5.3 Instant snapshot currently used in ChatGPT. Read more here.\nFebruary, 2026",
    "character_count": 946
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "1eae5abb-1b7d-4a73-9596-8461c06d033d",
    "technology": "openai_gpt",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.txt",
    "chunk_index": 12,
    "text": "Released gpt-5.3-chat-latest to the Chat Completions and Responses API. This model points to the GPT-5.3 Instant snapshot currently used in ChatGPT. Read more here.\nFebruary, 2026\nExpanded input_file support to accept more document, presentation, spreadsheet, code, and text file types. Learn more here.\nReleased phase to the Responses API. It labels an assistant message as intermediate commentary (commentary) or the final answer (final_answer). Read more here.\nReleased gpt-5.3-codex to the Responses API. Read more here.\nLaunched WebSocket mode for the Responses API. Learn more here.\nReleased GPT-Realtime-1.5 to the Realtime API.\nReleased gpt-audio-1.5 to the Chat Completions API. Read more here.\nBatch API is now supported for GPT Image models: gpt-image-1.5, chatgpt-image-latest, gpt-image-1, and gpt-image-1-mini.\nUpdated the gpt-5.2-chat-latest slug to point to the latest model currently used in ChatGPT.\nLaunched server-side compaction in the Responses API.",
    "character_count": 971
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "b5504eda-b620-47f6-841f-c382032e7cff",
    "technology": "openai_gpt",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.txt",
    "chunk_index": 13,
    "text": "Updated the gpt-5.2-chat-latest slug to point to the latest model currently used in ChatGPT.\nLaunched server-side compaction in the Responses API.\nLaunched support for Skills in the Responses API. We support Skills across both local execution and hosted container-based execution.\nLaunched a new Hosted Shell tool, as well as support for networking in containers.\nAdded support for application/json requests on /v1/images/edits for GPT image models. JSON requests use images (and optional mask) with image_url or file_id references instead of multipart uploads.\nWe have optimized our inference stack for API customers and GPT-5.2 and GPT-5.2-Codex now run ~40% faster. Model and model weights are unchanged.\nJanuary, 2026\nAnnounced Open Responses: an open-source spec for building multi-provider, interoperable LLM interfaces built on top of the original OpenAI Responses API.",
    "character_count": 876
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "a3b91f77-b7ec-4912-b365-c15884f59283",
    "technology": "openai_gpt",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.txt",
    "chunk_index": 14,
    "text": "January, 2026\nAnnounced Open Responses: an open-source spec for building multi-provider, interoperable LLM interfaces built on top of the original OpenAI Responses API.\nReleased gpt-5.2-codex to the Responses API. GPT-5.2-Codex is a version of GPT-5.2 optimized for agentic coding tasks in Codex or similar environments. Read more here.\nAdded dedicated SIP IP ranges for Realtime API. sip.api.openai.com does GeoIP routing, and will direct SIP traffic to the closest region. Learn more.\nUpdated the gpt-realtime-mini and gpt-audio-mini slugs to point to the 2025-12-15 snapshots. If you need the previous model snapshots, use gpt-realtime-mini-2025-10-06 and gpt-audio-mini-2025-10-06.\nUpdated the sora-2 slug to point to sora-2-2025-12-08. If you need the previous model snapshot, use sora-2-2025-10-06.",
    "character_count": 804
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "62793a12-0f26-4c88-8dec-747bd7171436",
    "technology": "openai_gpt",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.txt",
    "chunk_index": 15,
    "text": "Updated the sora-2 slug to point to sora-2-2025-12-08. If you need the previous model snapshot, use sora-2-2025-10-06.\nUpdated the gpt-4o-mini-tts and gpt-4o-mini-transcribe slugs to point to the 2025-12-15 snapshots. If you need the previous model snapshots, use gpt-4o-mini-tts-2025-03-20 and gpt-4o-mini-transcribe-2025-03-20. We currently recomend using gpt-4o-mini-transcribe over gpt-4o-transcribe for the best results.\nFixed an issue where gpt-image-1.5 and chatgpt-image-latest were incorrectly using high fidelity for image edits through /v1/images/edits, even when fidelity was explicitly set to low (the default).\nDecember, 2025\nAdded gpt-image-1.5 and chatgpt-image-latest to the Responses API image generation tool.\nReleased gpt-image-1.5 and chatgpt-image-latest, our latest and most advanced models for image generation. Read more here.",
    "character_count": 851
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "8acfac9d-4f0e-444f-97a3-3770d5812936",
    "technology": "openai_gpt",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.txt",
    "chunk_index": 16,
    "text": "Released gpt-image-1.5 and chatgpt-image-latest, our latest and most advanced models for image generation. Read more here.\nReleased four new dated audio snapshots. These updates deliver reliability, quality, and voice fidelity improvements for real-time, voice-driven applications. Read more here.\n- gpt-realtime-mini-2025-12-15\n- gpt-audio-mini-2025-12-15\n- gpt-4o-mini-transcribe-2025-12-15\n- gpt-4o-mini-tts-2025-12-15\nThis launch also includes support for Custom voices for eligible customers.\nReleased GPT-5.2, the newest flagship model in the GPT-5 model family. GPT-5.2 shows improvements over the previous GPT-5.1 in:\n- General intelligence\n- Instruction following\n- Accuracy and token efficiency\n- Multimodality—especially vision\n- Code generation—especially front-end UI creation\n- Tool calling and context management in the API\n- Spreadsheet understanding and creation.",
    "character_count": 880
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "d44d2d69-c85e-4d56-a2a4-f442954aaf0d",
    "technology": "openai_gpt",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.txt",
    "chunk_index": 17,
    "text": "- Multimodality—especially vision\n- Code generation—especially front-end UI creation\n- Tool calling and context management in the API\n- Spreadsheet understanding and creation.\nWhat's new in 5.2 is a new xhigh reasoning effort level, concise reasoning summaries, and new context management using compaction.\nReleased client-side compaction. For long-running conversations with the Responses API, you can use the /responses/compact endpoint to shrink the context you send with each turn.\nReleased gpt-5.1-codex-max to the Responses API. GPT-5.1-Codex is our most intelligent coding model optimized for long-horizon, agentic coding tasks. Read more here.\nNovember, 2025\nAdded support for DTMF key presses in the Realtime API. You can now receive DTMF events while using a Realtime sideband connection. See docs here for more information.\nReleased GPT-5.1, the newest flagship model in the GPT-5 model family. GPT-5.1 is trained to be especially proficient in:",
    "character_count": 956
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "b1adf125-a269-40e4-9dc5-80969eb4527f",
    "technology": "openai_gpt",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.txt",
    "chunk_index": 18,
    "text": "Released GPT-5.1, the newest flagship model in the GPT-5 model family. GPT-5.1 is trained to be especially proficient in:\n- Steerability and faster responses when less thinking's required\n- Code generation and coding use cases\n- Agentic workflows\nNote that GPT-5.1 defaults to a new none reasoning setting for faster responses when less thinking's required—different from the previous medium default setting in GPT-5.\nReleased enhanced role-based access controls (RBAC). Role-based access control (RBAC) lets you decide who can do what across your organization and projects—both through the API and in the Dashboard.\nReleased gpt-5.1-codex and gpt-5.1-codex-mini to the Responses API. GPT-5.1-Codex is a version of GPT-5.1 optimized for agentic coding tasks in Codex or similar environments. Read more here.",
    "character_count": 807
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "f5335ff9-2829-444d-8880-5d0f080b74bf",
    "technology": "openai_gpt",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.txt",
    "chunk_index": 19,
    "text": "Released gpt-5.1-codex and gpt-5.1-codex-mini to the Responses API. GPT-5.1-Codex is a version of GPT-5.1 optimized for agentic coding tasks in Codex or similar environments. Read more here.\nReleased extended prompt cache retention. Extended prompt cache retention keeps cached prefixes active for longer, up to a maximum of 24 hours. Extended Prompt Caching works by offloading the key/value tensors to GPU-local storage when memory is full, significantly increasing the storage capacity available for caching.\nOctober, 2025\ngpt-oss-safeguard-120b and gpt-oss-safeguard-20b are safety reasoning models built-upon gpt-oss. Read more here.\nReleased Enterprise Key Management (EKM). Enterprise Key Management (EKM) allows you to encrypt your customer content at OpenAI using keys managed by your own external Key Management System (KMS).\nReleased UK data residency.\nReleased several new features at OpenAI DevDay:",
    "character_count": 911
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "e947874d-6138-4450-ab64-1755ea2f7189",
    "technology": "openai_gpt",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.txt",
    "chunk_index": 20,
    "text": "Released UK data residency.\nReleased several new features at OpenAI DevDay:\nReleased GPT-5 Pro, a version of GPT-5 that uses more compute to think harder and provide consistently better answers.\nReleased GPT-Realtime mini and gpt-audio-mini for more cost-efficient speech to speech performance.\nReleased gpt-image-1-mini for more cost-efficient image generation and editing.\nLaunched v1/videos for rich, detailed, and dynamic video generation and remixing with our latest Sora 2 and Sora 2 Pro models.\nLaunched Agent Builder for visually creating custom multi-agent workflows.\nLaunched ChatKit, an embeddable chat interface for deploying agents.\nReleased Trace Evals, Datasets, and Prompt Optimization tools.\nEvals: Released Third-Party Model Support.\nLaunched Service health dashboard.\nReleased IP allowlist. IP allowlisting restricts API access to only the IP addresses or ranges you specify.\nSeptember, 2025\nAdded support for image and file as a tool call output in Responses API.",
    "character_count": 983
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "60fb35b3-57dc-4201-a09c-7a2bed40f3fa",
    "technology": "openai_gpt",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.txt",
    "chunk_index": 21,
    "text": "Released IP allowlist. IP allowlisting restricts API access to only the IP addresses or ranges you specify.\nSeptember, 2025\nAdded support for image and file as a tool call output in Responses API.\nLaunched special-purpose model gpt-5-codex, built and optimized for use with the Codex CLI.\nAugust, 2025\nThe OpenAI Realtime API is now generally available. Learn more in our Realtime API guide.\nAdded support for connectors to the Responses API. Connectors are OpenAI-maintained MCP wrappers for popular services like Google apps, Dropbox, and more that can be used to give model read access to data stored in those services.\nReleased the Conversations API, which allows you to create and manage long-running conversations with the Responses API. See the migration guide to see a side-by-side comparison and learn how to migrate from an Assistants API integration to Responses and Conversations.\nReleased GPT-5 family of models in the API, including gpt-5, gpt-5-mini, and gpt-5-nano.",
    "character_count": 981
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "3625744e-5a73-4c9a-8bf3-e49249286f29",
    "technology": "openai_gpt",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.txt",
    "chunk_index": 22,
    "text": "Released GPT-5 family of models in the API, including gpt-5, gpt-5-mini, and gpt-5-nano.\nIntroduced the minimal reasoning effort value to optimize for fast responses in GPT-5 models (which support reasoning).\nIntroduced custom tool call type, which allows for freeform inputs to and outputs from the model when tool calling.\nJune, 2025\nLaunched support for Priority processing. Priority processing delivers significantly lower and more consistent latency compared to Standard processing while keeping pay-as-you-go flexibility.\nReleased o3-deep-research and o4-mini-deep-research, deep research variants of our o-series reasoning models optimized for deep analysis and research tasks. Learn more in the deep research guide.\nAdded support for async event handling with webhooks. Reduced and simplified pricing for the web search tool. Added support for the web search tool.",
    "character_count": 872
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "37f6027e-a065-428a-bb9d-3381fc5d63ee",
    "technology": "openai_gpt",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.txt",
    "chunk_index": 23,
    "text": "Added support for async event handling with webhooks. Reduced and simplified pricing for the web search tool. Added support for the web search tool.\nNew reusable prompts are now available in the dashboard and Responses API. Via API, you can now reference templates created in the dashboard via the prompt parameter (with a prompt id, optional version) and supply dynamic variables that can include strings, images, or file inputs. Reusable prompts are not available in Chat Completions. Learn more.\nReleased o3-pro, a version of the o3 reasoning model that uses more compute to answer hard problems with better reasoning and consistency. Prices for the o3 model have also been reduced for all API requests, including batch and flex processing.\nAdded fine-tuning support with direct preference optimization for the models gpt-4.1-2025-04-14, gpt-4.1-mini-2025-04-14, and gpt-4.1-nano-2025-04-14.",
    "character_count": 894
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "ee15883d-5590-44d0-8efb-ce44993f865e",
    "technology": "openai_gpt",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.txt",
    "chunk_index": 24,
    "text": "Added fine-tuning support with direct preference optimization for the models gpt-4.1-2025-04-14, gpt-4.1-mini-2025-04-14, and gpt-4.1-nano-2025-04-14.\nNew model snapshots available for gpt-4o-audio-preview and gpt-4o-realtime-preview. Released Agents SDK for TypeScript.\nMay, 2025\nAdded support for new built-in tools in the Responses API, including remote MCP servers and code interpreter. Learn more about tools.\nAdded support for using strict mode for tool schemas when using parallel tool calling with non-fine-tuned models.\nAdded new schema features, including string validation for email and other patterns and specifying ranges for numbers and arrays.\nLaunched codex-mini-latest in the API, optimized for use with the Codex CLI.\nLaunched support for reinforcement fine-tuning. Learn about available fine-tuning methods. gpt-4.1-nano is now available for fine-tuning.\nApril, 2025\nLaunched support for Enhanced API Budget Alerts & Auto-recharge Limits.",
    "character_count": 957
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "2715bd98-3da4-4c89-8f58-ae2cef432cb9",
    "technology": "openai_gpt",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.txt",
    "chunk_index": 25,
    "text": "April, 2025\nLaunched support for Enhanced API Budget Alerts & Auto-recharge Limits.\nAdded a new image generation model, gpt-image-1. This model sets a new standard for image generation, with improved quality and instruction following.\nUpdated the Image Generation and Edit endpoints to support new parameters specific to the gpt-image-1 model.\nAdded two new o-series reasoning models, o3 and o4-mini. They set a new standard for math, science, and coding, visual reasoning tasks, and technical writing.\nLaunched Codex, our code generation CLI tool.\nAdded gpt-4.1, gpt-4.1-mini, and gpt-4.1-nano models to the API. These new models feature improved instruction following, coding, and a larger context window (up to 1M tokens). gpt-4.1 and gpt-4.1-mini are available for supervised fine-tuning. Announced deprecation of gpt-4.5-preview.\nMarch, 2025\nAdded gpt-4o-mini-tts, gpt-4o-transcribe, gpt-4o-mini-transcribe, and whisper-1 models to the Audio API.",
    "character_count": 951
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "d102dbd3-d5b5-4679-8d06-f899d81364fe",
    "technology": "openai_gpt",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.txt",
    "chunk_index": 26,
    "text": "March, 2025\nAdded gpt-4o-mini-tts, gpt-4o-transcribe, gpt-4o-mini-transcribe, and whisper-1 models to the Audio API.\nReleased several new models and tools and a new API for agentic workflows:\n- Released the Responses API, a new API for creating and using agents and tools.\n- Released a set of built-in tools for the Responses API: web search, file search, and computer use.\n- Released the Agents SDK, an orchestration framework for designing, building, and deploying agents.\n- Announced new models: gpt-4o-search-preview,gpt-4o-mini-search-preview,computer-use-preview.\n- Announced plans to bring all Assistants API features to the easier to use Responses API, with an anticipated sunset date for Assistants in 2026 (after achieving full feature parity).\nAdded metadata field support to fine-tuning jobs.\nFebruary, 2025",
    "character_count": 819
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "961f735f-0ae7-4ded-92bc-8fb9691588dd",
    "technology": "openai_gpt",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.txt",
    "chunk_index": 27,
    "text": "Added metadata field support to fine-tuning jobs.\nFebruary, 2025\nReleased a research preview of GPT-4.5—our largest and most capable chat model yet. GPT-4.5's high \"EQ\" and understanding of user intent make it better at creative tasks and agentic planning.\nLaunched the API Usage Dashboard Update. This update addresses requests for additional data filters, such as project selection, date picker, and fine-grained intervals. There’s also better support for viewing usage across different products and service tiers.\nIntroducing data residency in Europe. Read more here.\nJanuary, 2025\nLaunched o3-mini, a new small reasoning model that is optimized for science, math, and coding tasks.\nExpanded access to o1 model. The o1 series of models are trained with reinforcement learning to perform complex reasoning.\nDecember, 2024\nLaunched Admin API Key Rotations, enabling customers to programmatically rotate their admin api keys.",
    "character_count": 925
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "bb74de01-4fbd-4ad6-ad86-d18dbdea8c62",
    "technology": "openai_gpt",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.txt",
    "chunk_index": 28,
    "text": "December, 2024\nLaunched Admin API Key Rotations, enabling customers to programmatically rotate their admin api keys.\nUpdated Admin API Invites, enabling customers to programmatically invite users to projects at the same time they are invited to organizations.\nAdded new models for o1, gpt-4o-realtime, gpt-4o-audio and more.\nAdded WebRTC connection method for the Realtime API.\nAdded reasoning_effort parameter for o1 models.\nAdded developer message role for o1 model. Note that o1-preview and o1-mini do not support system or developer messages.\nLaunched Preference Fine-tuning using Direct Preference Optimization (DPO).\nLaunched beta SDKs for Go and Java. Learn more.\nAdded Realtime API support in the Python SDK.\nLaunched Usage API, enabling customers to programmatically query activities and spending across OpenAI APIs.\nNovember, 2024\nReleased gpt-4o-2024-11-20, our newest model in the gpt-4o series.",
    "character_count": 907
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "c089dddc-6fe6-4bc6-9f88-83f726f46362",
    "technology": "openai_gpt",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.txt",
    "chunk_index": 29,
    "text": "Launched Usage API, enabling customers to programmatically query activities and spending across OpenAI APIs.\nNovember, 2024\nReleased gpt-4o-2024-11-20, our newest model in the gpt-4o series.\nReleased Predicted Outputs, which greatly reduces latency for model responses where much of the response is known ahead of time. This is most common when regenerating the content of documents and code files with only minor changes.\nOctober, 2024\nAdded five new voice types in the Realtime API and Chat Completions API.\nReleased new gpt-4o-audio-preview model for chat completions, which supports both audio inputs and outputs. Uses the same underlying model as the Realtime API.\nReleased several new features at OpenAI DevDay in San Francisco:\nRealtime API: Build fast speech-to-speech experiences into your applications using a WebSockets interface.\nModel distillation: Platform for fine-tuning cost-efficient models with your outputs from a large frontier model.",
    "character_count": 955
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "046613a9-c13e-4ba2-bb24-17a4108612b2",
    "technology": "openai_gpt",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.txt",
    "chunk_index": 30,
    "text": "Model distillation: Platform for fine-tuning cost-efficient models with your outputs from a large frontier model.\nImage fine-tuning: Fine-tune GPT-4o with images and text to improve vision capabilities.\nEvals: Create and run custom evaluations to measure model performance on specific tasks.\nPrompt caching: Discounts and faster processing times on recently seen input tokens.\nGenerate in playground: Easily generate prompts, function definitions, and structured output schemas in the playground using the Generate button.\nSeptember, 2024\nReleased new omni-moderation-latest moderation model, which supports both images and text (for some categories), supports two new text-only harm categories, and has more accurate scores.\nReleased o1-preview and o1-mini, new large language models trained with reinforcement learning to perform complex reasoning tasks.\nAugust, 2024\nAssistants API now supports including file search results used by the file search tool, and customizing ranking behavior.",
    "character_count": 991
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "ea1cc9fa-cba5-4c97-bec4-ff02e5310497",
    "technology": "openai_gpt",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.txt",
    "chunk_index": 31,
    "text": "August, 2024\nAssistants API now supports including file search results used by the file search tool, and customizing ranking behavior.\nGA release for gpt-4o-2024-08-06 fine-tuning—all API users can now fine-tune the latest GPT-4o model.\nReleased dynamic model for chatgpt-4o-latest—this model will point to the latest GPT-4o model used by ChatGPT.\nLaunched Structured Outputs—model outputs now reliably adhere to developer supplied JSON Schemas.\nReleased gpt-4o-2024-08-06, our newest model in the gpt-4o series.\nLaunched Admin and Audit Log APIs, allowing customers to programmatically administer their organization and monitor changes using the audit logs. Audit logging must be enabled within settings.\nJuly, 2024\nLaunched self-serve SSO configuration, allowing Enterprise customers on custom and unlimited billing to set up authentication against their desired IDP.\nLaunched fine-tuning for GPT-4o mini, enabling even higher performance for specific use cases.",
    "character_count": 964
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "16434fd5-79c9-4f5d-b139-89ebdd23988b",
    "technology": "openai_gpt",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.txt",
    "chunk_index": 32,
    "text": "Launched fine-tuning for GPT-4o mini, enabling even higher performance for specific use cases.\nReleased GPT-4o mini, our affordable an intelligent small model for fast, lightweight tasks.\nReleased Uploads to upload large files in multiple parts.\nJune, 2024\nParallel function calling can be disabled in Chat Completions and the Assistants API by passing parallel_tool_calls=false.\n.NET SDK launched in Beta.\nAdded support for file search customizations.\nMay, 2024\nAdded support for archiving projects . Only organization owners can access this functionality.\nAdded support for setting cost limits on a per-project basis for pay as you go customers.\nReleased GPT-4o in the API. GPT-4o is our fastest and most affordable flagship model.\nAdded support for image inputs to the Assistants API.\nAdded support for fine-tuned models to the Batch API .",
    "character_count": 842
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "68ba57ec-e0c7-4961-83be-80557cfd878c",
    "technology": "openai_gpt",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.txt",
    "chunk_index": 33,
    "text": "Released GPT-4o in the API. GPT-4o is our fastest and most affordable flagship model.\nAdded support for image inputs to the Assistants API.\nAdded support for fine-tuned models to the Batch API .\nAdded stream_options: {\"include_usage\": true} parameter to the Chat Completions and Completions APIs. Setting this gives developers access to usage stats when using streaming.\nAdded a new endpoint to delete a message from a thread in the Assistants API.\nApril, 2024\nAdded a new function calling option tool_choice: \"required\" to the Chat Completions and Assistants APIs.\nAdded a guide for the Batch API and Batch API support for embeddings models\nIntroduced a series of updates to the Assistants API , including a new file search tool allowing up to 10,000 files per assistant, new token controls, and support for tool choice.",
    "character_count": 821
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "410ab094-d7e6-4f66-a782-dc1269555b91",
    "technology": "openai_gpt",
    "source": "release_notes",
    "path": "openai_gpt/release_notes.txt",
    "chunk_index": 34,
    "text": "Introduced a series of updates to the Assistants API , including a new file search tool allowing up to 10,000 files per assistant, new token controls, and support for tool choice.\nIntroduced project based hierarchy for organizing work by projects, including the ability to create API keys and manage rate and cost limits on a per-project basis (cost limits available only for Enterprise customers).\nReleased Batch API\nReleased GPT-4 Turbo with Vision in general availability in the API\nAdded support for seed in the fine-tuning API\nAdded support for checkpoints in the fine-tuning API\nAdded support for adding Messages when creating a Run in the Assistants API\nAdded support for filtering Messages by run_id in the Assistants API\nMarch, 2024\nAdded support for temperature and assistant message creation in the Assistants API\nAdded support for streaming in the Assistants API\nJanuary, 2024\nReleased embedding V3 models and an updated GPT-4 Turbo preview",
    "character_count": 952
  },
