    "path": "sentence_transformers/api_reference.txt",
    "chunk_index": 29,
    "text": "- inputs – The inputs to embed. Can be a string, a list of strings, or multimodal inputs (dicts, images, arrays).\n- prompt_name (str, optional) – The name of the prompt to use for encoding. Must be a key in the - promptsdictionary, which is either set in the constructor or loaded from the model configuration. For example if- prompt_nameis “query” and the- promptsis {“query”: “query: “, …}, then the sentence “What is the capital of France?” will be encoded as “query: What is the capital of France?” because the sentence is appended to the prompt. If- promptis also set, this argument is ignored. Defaults to None.\n- prompt (str, optional) – The prompt to use for encoding. For example, if the prompt is “query: “, then the sentence “What is the capital of France?” will be encoded as “query: What is the capital of France?” because the sentence is appended to the prompt. If - promptis set,- prompt_nameis ignored. Defaults to None.",
    "character_count": 936
  },
