    "text": "- supports(modality: Literal['text', 'image', 'audio', 'video', 'message'] | tuple[Literal['text', 'image', 'audio', 'video'], ...]) bool\n- Check if the model supports the given modality. - A modality is supported if: - It is directly listed in - modalities(including tuple modalities that are explicitly listed), or\n- It is a tuple of modalities (e.g. - (\"image\", \"text\")) where each part is individually supported and the model also supports- \"message\"format, which is used to combine multiple modalities into a single input.\n- Parameters:\n- modality – A single modality string (e.g. - \"text\",- \"image\") or a tuple of modality strings (e.g.- (\"image\", \"text\")).\n- Returns:\n- Whether the model supports the given modality.\n- Return type:\n- bool\n- Example: - >>> from sentence_transformers import SentenceTransformer >>> model = SentenceTransformer(\"sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2\") >>> model.supports(\"text\") True >>> model.supports(\"image\") False\n- to(*args, **kwargs)",
