  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "fb21d3cd-32c1-4f41-9c38-02880968462f",
    "technology": "sentence_transformers",
    "source": "official_documentation",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/official_documentation.txt",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "text": "Tip\nSentence Transformers v5.5 recently released, introducing the train-sentence-transformers Agent Skill. Using an AI coding agent (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Gemini CLI, …)? Install it via hf skills add train-sentence-transformers [--global] [--claude] and ask your agent to train or finetune an embedding, reranker, or sparse encoder model on your data. See the v5.5.0 Release Notes for more details.\nSentenceTransformers Documentation\nSentence Transformers (a.k.a. SBERT) is the go-to Python module for using and training state-of-the-art embedding and reranker models. It can be used to compute embeddings from text, images, audio, or video using Sentence Transformer models (quickstart), to calculate similarity scores using Cross-Encoder (a.k.a. reranker) models (quickstart), or to generate sparse embeddings using Sparse Encoder models (quickstart). This unlocks a wide range of applications, including semantic search, semantic textual similarity, and paraphrase mining.",
    "character_count": 981
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "94c231a6-67ed-40cb-84b2-35e66d3c7bb8",
    "technology": "sentence_transformers",
    "source": "official_documentation",
    "path": "sentence_transformers/official_documentation.txt",
    "chunk_index": 1,
    "text": "A wide selection of over 10,000 pre-trained Sentence Transformers models are available for immediate use on 🤗 Hugging Face, including many of the state-of-the-art models from the Massive Text Embeddings Benchmark (MTEB) leaderboard. Additionally, it is easy to train or finetune your own embedding models, reranker models, or sparse encoder models using Sentence Transformers, enabling you to create custom models for your specific use cases.\nSentence Transformers was created by UKP Lab and is being maintained by 🤗 Hugging Face. Don’t hesitate to open an issue on the Sentence Transformers repository if something is broken or if you have further questions.\nUsage\nSee also\nSee the Quickstart for more quick information on how to use Sentence Transformers.\nWorking with Sentence Transformer models is straightforward:\nfrom sentence_transformers import SentenceTransformer\n# 1. Load a pretrained Sentence Transformer model\nmodel = SentenceTransformer(\"sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2\")",
    "character_count": 992
  },
  {
    "chunk_id": "1498b194-2667-44f2-9a3c-1102cb9f7a9d",
